  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to Labour Behind the Label</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Labour Behind the Label supports garment workers&apos; efforts worldwide to defend their rights. They educate consumers, lobby companies and government, raise awareness, and encourage international solidarity with workers. In addition, they coordinate the UK platform of the international Clean Clothes Campaign.

In 2010 the Ethical Trading Initiative is prioritising work in support of living wages in global supply chains. Traditionally it has proved very difficult to make progress even with ETI member companies on this issue, although it is a priority for workers in developing countries. LBL will keep up the external pressure through campaigns asking high street companies to ensure that their suppliers pay a living wage and by linking in with workers organisations in Asia through the Asian Floor Wage campaign. The aim of this grant is to support LBL in their work on living wages and ensure that they are working strategically with NGO members of ETI to exert maximum influence over company policies.</narrative>
  </description>
